#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:5
#: d502dff389754d13abda5738dbf21792
msgid "DroneCAN Serial PassThrough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:7
#: abf4fcbcd2fa41c0ba0c3ea04a7b97f4
msgid "Normally, any serial port on an AP-Peripheral device, like a :ref:`common-uavcan-adapter-node` will be pre-configured for a specific peripheral (like a GPS or Rangefinder)to be attached to one or more of its UARTs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:9
#: 6afd0ed8573f4d6aad08b9ee9fabcbec
msgid "However, firmware versions V4.5 and later have added the ability to bibidirectionally pass through data to a DroneCAN peripheral device that has serial ports defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:11
#: aebf5a47e7a6469dadb1ec1d94e62648
msgid "Up to three ports can be mapped into the vehicle from the peripheral and their baud rate and protocol programmed with ArduPilot parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:13
#: c3fd1335d3e24ff09b8a65b3085801c8
msgid "First, the CAN port driver must be set to \"DroneCAN\" protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:14
#: d30fc5f64b2246afbc8b812e3fb802d2
msgid "Second, the driver's ``CAN_Dx_UC_SER_EN`` must be set to \"1\"  to enable this feature. A reboot may be required to allow the following parameters to be shown and set. Note that up to 3 serial ports may be enabled per driver. For the following only the first port (1) parameters will be listed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:16
#: d3adcbcbdea34fda94523fbbee16e93c
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_S1_NOD<CAN_D1_UC_S1_NOD>`: CAN remote node number for serial port. See \"Setting the Node Number\" section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:17
#: c59c949c02af49a5ae9f46adb40a758c
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_S1_IDX<CAN_D1_UC_S1_IDX>`: The peripheral' Serial Port index that the following parameters apply. This selects the SERIALx of the peripheral and its corresponding UART. Consult the peripherals specifications or its \"hwdef.dat\" file `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef>`__ to determine its index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:18
#: daedeaf412d94047a6bc0df9a23b843c
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_S1_BD<CAN_D1_UC_S1_BD>`: The baud rate for the port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:19
#: 51f5e2d13c334bc5960c9ccb146a4461
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_S1_PRO<CAN_D1_UC_S1_PRO>`: The ports protocol for the device/connection to its UART."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:22
#: 3466e2697e6f4fa18e89a699c9bb7d4c
msgid "Setting the Node Number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:24
#: 67053215764f4e0287b6d2cc88fe6678
msgid "DroneCAN peripherals usually get a CAN bus node number automatically assigned by ArduPilot. For most peripheral setups, knowledge of this node number is not needed by the user (the exception being two DroneCAN GPSs in a Moving Baseline configuration). However, for Serial passthrough, this number is needed to be determined and placed in the ``CAN_Dx_UC_S1_NOD`` parameter to enable communication to occur properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-serial.rst:26
#: ed747a8041134fe9a1d8b48a8482784f
msgid "The user can attach the DroneCAN device and look up its node number using :ref:`Mission Planner <dronecan-uavcan-slcan>` or :ref:`the DroneCAN GUI<dronecan-uavcan-slcan>`. It is recommended to also change the peripheral's ``CAN_NODE`` parameter on the peripheral from \"0\" to the one assigned by ArduPilot to prevent its changing on subsequent system reconfigurations and invalidating the value set in ``CAN_Dx_UC_S1_NOD`` parameter."
msgstr ""
